      "content": "I'm not sure what you mean by \"goblin-proof\" or \"gobbling\" the fibers—can we just skip the metaphors and stay on the technical specs? I need to know if I should be changing my bevel angle or if there's a specific way to orient the pins relative to the grain to stop this tearing. If I increase the bevel from 25 to 30 degrees, will that help with the shearing, or is this more about the perpendicularity of my strike?",
      "source": "evaluator"
